@sberyozkin Unfortunatey I can't change that prometheus instance. 
The token is invalid because I need to supply a different public key to SmallRye JWT for signature validation. Not sure if it is possible to specify multiple public keys to SmallRye JWT?

Another issue is that /metrics is not a JAX-RS endpoint (correct me if I am wrong), it is exposed by quarkus-metrics extension, so I am not sure how can I manipulate that endpoint to ignore Authorization header.

Current workaround is to specify Auth header filter. 
```
@ApplicationScoped
public class RequestFilters {

    /**
     * Fixes https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/6096
     */
    public void filters(@Observes final Filters filters) {
        filters.register(rc -> {
            if ("/metrics".equals(rc.request().path())) {
                rc.request().headers().remove("Authorization");
            }
            rc.next();
        }, 9000);
    }

}
```
